cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MixConfig in your research, please cite the ICML 2026 paper below."
title: "MixConfig: Mixing Configurations for Downstream Prediction"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Q9gJYx/MixConfig"
url: "https://openreview.net/forum?id=MomisBwZhT"
abstract: >-
  MixConfig is a plug-and-play feature augmentation module that extracts
  structurally stable clustering configurations from a frozen embedding and
  learns energy-aware mixing weights per sample for downstream prediction.
keywords:
  - multi-resolution clustering
  - configuration mixing
  - graph-based features
  - feature augmentation
  - low-data learning
